      "kind": "fight",
      "text": "A few steps into the fog, the wet grass at the roadside erupts — a rat the size of a cat, hackles up, lunging straight for your ankle.\n\nYou jab the cane at it and catch it hard across the flank; it shrieks and reels back, 5 left in it.\n\nYou strike again before it recovers, a solid crack across its spine; 4 left in it.\n\nYou swing wide and it's already inside your reach, needle teeth sinking into your calf — 99 left of you.\n\nYou plant your foot to drive the next blow and it slides out from under you in the wet grass, and the rat is on you before you're set, tearing at your forearm — 96 left of you.\n\nOff balance, you still get the cane down on it, a heavy blow that folds it sideways, 2 left in it.\n\nYou lunge to finish it and miss your footing again, and it darts in and bites, 95 left of you.",
